    "constraints": [
      "declare only the workflow: SY.wf-rules packages it and creates and runs its node, WF.<workflow_name>@<hive>",
      "workflow_name is lowercase letters, digits and '-' in dot-separated parts, each starting with a letter, and unique per hive",
      "the definition is a wf_schema_version 1 state machine: workflow_type, start_from, input_schema, initial_state, terminal_states, states with entry_actions, exit_actions and transitions (CEL guards), and an optional catch",
      "a definition names in start_from the nodes whose messages start an instance: IO nodes or WFs, each a node name with its hive, never an AI.* node (an agent only answers) nor a SY.* or RT.* node; only the nodes written in it drive an instance: those of start_from, of an event_match.src, and the targets of its send_message and forward actions, the catch's included",
      "every message a WF sends is a user message: an action's meta has msg and context, never type",
      "a send_message target is a node name written in the definition; to choose among destinations, write one transition per destination with its guard",
      "a WF asks an agent with a menu on a send_message or a forward to an AI.* node: an optional help, and 1 to 8 options, each a name, a description and optional typed params; the agent adds none, with the param reason",
      "an agent's answer to a menu has its reply, maybe empty, in event.payload.content, and {reply, option, params} in event.context.evaluation: branch on event.context.evaluation.option, and forward the answer to the IO node to give the person the reply",
      "an agent's error answer (an answer off the menu, a timeout, a provider failure) is a payload of type 'error', with no retry; its msg is <msg>.error only when the request had a msg (a forwarded person's message has none: match the agent by event_match.src, with the guard event.payload.type == 'error')",
      "what no transition of the current state takes goes to the catch, a top-level list of transitions tried in any state (sends, forwards, keep_message, set_variable and emit_internal_event; no timers); what the catch does not take is logged as unhandled event, and the instance stays where it was",
      "at most 8 messages go to agents between two triggers (a message from an IO node or a WF, or a timer's fire): past that the send is not made, and the instance gets one AGENT_CALL_CAP event, a payload of type 'error'",
      "a timer's key is event.timer_key: a timeout is a TIMER_FIRED transition with the guard event.timer_key == '<timer_key>'",
      "a $ref to a field that may be missing gives a default: {\"$ref\": \"event.context\", \"default\": {}}; a $ref without one fails the instance"
    ],
    "do_not_repeat": [
      "do not declare the WF node in nodes, nor a runtime for it: SY.wf-rules makes both",
      "do not put the workflow definition content inside a node config — it goes in wf_deployments",
      "do not deploy a workflow on an ingress or egress hive: it has no SY.wf-rules",
      "do not write meta.type, target_ref, thread_id_ref, meta.context.response_envelope or event.payload.timer_key: SY.wf-rules refuses the first four, and the fifth is never set",
      "do not put routing rules in an agent's role: the WF hands the agent a menu with each message, and the role keeps only the agent's trade",
      "do not name a menu option none, nor read an option or a param that no menu of the definition has: SY.wf-rules refuses both",
      "do not forward an agent's empty reply to an IO node: guard that forward with event.context.evaluation.reply != ''",
      "do not ask an agent again with the same message: deliver its answer, then wait for the person's next message",
      "do not wait for an answer without a timer: an agent or a node that never answers leaves the instance waiting forever"
    ],
    "failure_class": null,
    "recorded_from_run": null,
    "seed_kind": "manual",
    "seed_version": 4
  }
